# The autosave dialog, held open.
#
# The dialog is the first thing the game draws: a bordered window that opens
# with a horizontal expansion animation and then sits waiting for A. Pressing
# nothing keeps it up for the whole run, so a capture can watch both the
# opening animation - which is where the window used to snap outwards the frame
# its body crossed 90% of the canvas - and the settled composition.
#
# Budget: the dialog is up from about 0.15e9 retired instructions. 2.5e9 gives
# roughly 250 VI fields of it.
label autosave-dialog
wait 2000
loop
